Spec: Aikana
Platform: Python/FastHTML/HTMX/SQLite/Tailwind CSS

Purpose:
  Aikana is a time-keeping and lesson calendar. A single admin (the teacher) records courses, course realizations,
  lessons and holidays. Unauthenticated students can only view the data. The calendar is presented as a semester
  wall planner and as a per-CourseRealization weekly calendar.

Structure:
  ./src/aikana/: the application package, with its entry point and feature packages for the domain entities,
    calendar views, auth and the MCP adapter
  ./tests/: automated tests
  ./data/: local-only directory mounted into the container at `/data`
  ./README.md: how to launch the app and how to connect an AI agent to its MCP endpoint
  ./CONTRIBUTE.md: how to develop iteratively with SpecDD
  ./Dockerfile: multi-stage image definition shared by local testing and production
  ./compose.yml: local run configuration that builds the `prod` stage and mounts `./data` at `/data`
  ./pyproject.toml: package metadata, dependencies and tool configuration
  ./uv.lock: locked dependency versions produced by `uv`

Owns:
  ./pyproject.toml
  ./uv.lock
  ./README.md
  ./CONTRIBUTE.md
  ./Dockerfile
  ./compose.yml
  ./.dockerignore
  ./.gitignore

References:
  ./src/aikana/architecture.sdd

Must:
  The SQLite database file lives at `/data/app.db` so that it can be mounted as a persistent volume.
  The admin password is read from the `AIKANA_PASSWD` environment variable and the listening port from `PORT`.
  The MCP write token is read from the `AIKANA_MCP_TOKEN` environment variable.
  Unauthenticated visitors can view all data and cannot create, change or delete anything.
  Only the authenticated admin (session login) or a caller presenting the `AIKANA_MCP_TOKEN` bearer token
    (./src/aikana/mcp_server/mcp_server.sdd) can write data.
  All UI text is in English.
  The application is used only in the `Europe/Helsinki` time zone: calendar dates, "today" and week boundaries are
  computed in Europe/Helsinki regardless of the host's time zone.
  Calendar dates are displayed in the European `d.m.yyyy` form (for example `2.10.2026`), never in the ISO
  `yyyy-mm-dd` or US `mm/dd/yyyy` form. The rule governs rendered views; the MCP machine interface in
  ./src/aikana/mcp_server/mcp_server.sdd uses ISO 8601 dates and times on the wire.
  Weeks start on Monday and week numbering follows the ISO 8601 European standard, where week `1` is the week that
  contains the year's first Thursday.
  Tailwind CSS is compiled ahead of time with the standalone Tailwind CLI in `Dockerfile`'s `css` stage (no
  Node.js/npm toolchain) and served as a static file; the Play CDN script (`cdn.tailwindcss.com`) must not be used.
  The CLI download is pinned to an exact version and verified against its SHA-256 checksum at build time, so the
  build never executes an unvetted upstream binary.
  Dependencies are declared in `pyproject.toml` and locked in `uv.lock`, and every Docker stage installs exactly the
  locked set with `uv`.
  `Dockerfile` has a `base` stage with the common setup, a `test` stage and a `prod` stage that both inherit from
  `base`. `test` installs the application the same way `prod` does, adds the `dev` dependency group, copies `./tests`
  and runs `pytest` during the build. `prod` is the last stage, so a plain `docker build` produces the production
  image without development dependencies or tests.
  `compose.yml` builds the `prod` stage through `target: prod`, so local runs exercise the deployed image.
  The container starts the app with `python -m aikana.main`, so no `Procfile` exists.
  The production deployment target is the Dokku app `aikana` on `ssh.munpaas.com`, served at
  `https://aikana.munpaas.com` with a TLS certificate managed by the `letsencrypt` plugin; its `/data` directory is
  backed by Dokku persistent storage, so the SQLite database survives redeploys and restarts; deployments are manual
  git pushes by the maintainer until an automated pipeline replaces them.
  The repository root contains no application source files.
  Development proceeds in small increments and every increment is tested locally in Docker first.

Must not:
  Nothing in the repository or its tooling may publish, push or deploy to Dokku or GitHub. The human decides when and
  how to do that.
  Secrets, including `AIKANA_PASSWD` values and database files, must not be committed.

Forbids:
  Any database other than SQLite.
  Any ORM other than `fastlite`'s MiniDataAPI Spec implementation, as detailed in ./src/aikana/architecture.sdd.
  Frontend frameworks other than HTMX and Tailwind CSS.

